-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Run the numbers</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Free, before you offer</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Run the numbers on a Myrtle Beach rental<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">before you offer.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated September 7, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Send one address. You get the numbers for that Myrtle Beach rental: rent, property tax at the 6 percent rate, insurance, dues, management and cash flow, free.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="#run-form">Send the address</a></div></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Send the address of a Myrtle Beach rental you are thinking about buying, and the plan you have for it. A licensed team member builds the numbers for that property. That means the rent it can earn, the property tax at the 6 percent rate, the insurance, the HOA dues, the management fee and the monthly cash flow. You get them the same day, free, with no obligation. The investor analyzer does a first pass on its own if you want to start there.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is a run-the-numbers request?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It is one address and one plan, sent to us before you offer. We build the purchase numbers for that property and send them back to you. It is the same work we do for a client before any offer, done before you decide whether to work with us.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The numbers are estimates for a buying decision. They are not an appraisal and not a loan quote. Your lender sets the loan terms and an appraiser sets the appraised value.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What do you get back?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">One sheet with the lines below, each with its source.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What you get</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where it comes from</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Rent the unit can earn</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Rented comparables from the MLS, and the unit&#39;s own rental history when the seller provides it.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Property tax</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The county&#39;s assessed value at the 6 percent rate for a property that is not your legal residence. <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">How Horry County property tax works</a>.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Insurance</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">An estimate for that address, with wind and flood where the zone requires it. <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Coastal insurance, explained</a>.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">HOA dues and what they cover</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The listing and the association documents. <a href="/hoa/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Our HOA guide</a>.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Management</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The fee for the plan you chose: the building&#39;s rental program, an outside company, or self-managed. <a href="/invest/condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Why we do not default to the on-site manager</a>.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Monthly cash flow and DSCR</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Rent minus every cost above and the loan. DSCR is the ratio your lender checks. <a href="/invest/strategies/dscr-loans/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">DSCR loans, explained</a>.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Rental rules at that address</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Whether nightly rentals are allowed there, by city and zone. <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The rules by city</a>.</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Building financing, for a condo</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Whether lenders finance that building. <a href="/invest/condotel-financing/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Condotel financing</a>.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="run-form"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What should you send?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The address is enough. Everything else helps.</p><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">The address, or the MLS number.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Your plan: long-term rental, short-term rental, mid-term rental or fix and flip. Not sure is fine.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">How you plan to pay, cash or a loan. We do not need your finances to run the property. <a href="/invest/cash-to-close/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">What you pay at closing, beyond the down payment</a>.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Whether you will stay in it yourself. More than 14 nights a year changes the tax treatment. <a href="/invest/14-day-rule/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The 14-day rule</a>.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem">Anything you already have: a rent history, the dues, a prior inspection.</li></ul><div id="rnWrap" style="max-width:680px;background:var(--ivory);border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:14px;padding:1.6rem;text-align:left;margin:1.4rem 0">
