-</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How long does it take?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most requests come back the same day, evenings included. A condo takes longer when the dues or the rental rules are only in the association documents, because we request them first. An address in a zone where nightly rentals need checking takes a call to the city.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You get the numbers by email. If you gave a phone number, you also get a call.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Can you run the numbers yourself first?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The investor analyzer</a> takes a price, a rent and the costs. It returns the monthly cash flow, the cap rate and the DSCR. The cap rate is the yearly net income divided by the price. The DSCR is the rent divided by the loan payment. <a href="/invest/str-tools/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The short-term rental tools</a> estimate nightly revenue by area.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A person adds three things the tools cannot: the rent a specific unit gets, the rules in that building, and an insurance figure for that address.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Already ran it through the analyzer?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Send the address and the number you got. We tell you what the tool could not see.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="#run-form">Send the address</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Why get the numbers from a local agent?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Agents at Chapter3 own rentals on the Grand Strand. Tim Nash has sold on this beach for more than 30 years. The rent comparables come from the same MLS we sell from, and the building rules come from the association documents.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A national site gives you averages. We give you the numbers for one address, from people who work here.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What happens after you send it?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A licensed team member reads the request and builds the sheet. You get it by email the same day, evenings included. If you gave a phone number, you get a call too.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If the numbers work, we can set up a showing or walk the property on video for you. If they do not work, we say so and you keep the sheet. You can send more than one address.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Run-the-numbers FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is running the numbers free?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. There is no fee and no obligation. You can send one address or several.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do I need to be working with Chapter3 already?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Send the address and we build the numbers. You decide afterwards whether to work with us.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you run numbers on a property listed with another brokerage?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Any property for sale on the Grand Strand. We use the listing, the county record, rental comparables and the association documents.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What if the property is not for sale yet?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Send it anyway. We run numbers on a property you already own or one you are watching.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Will you call me?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only if you give a phone number. Leave it blank and we answer by email.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/assessor/guide-to-assessment/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Assessor, Guide to Assessment</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/publications/p527" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Publication 527, residential rental property</a>. Read September 6, 2026. The numbers we send are estimates for a buying decision, not an appraisal or a loan quote.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">One address is enough to start.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">Send it and a licensed team member returns the numbers the same day, evenings included.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="#run-form">Send the address</a></div></section></main>
+</script><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo can take longer when the dues or the rental rules are only in the association's papers, because we request them first. If the numbers work, we can set up a showing or walk the home on video for you. If they do not, we say so, and you keep the sheet.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="rental-numbers-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Rental numbers FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is there a free rental property calculator for Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, the one on this page. It uses HUD's rent for the ZIP code, the 6 percent rate and school tax for the town, the HOA dues, and our allowances for management, repairs and empty months.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Beach a good place to buy a rental property?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For cash flow alone, rarely by the national rules: 14 of 2,975 houses for sale pass the 1 percent rule, and Longs and Carolina Forest come closest. The tax a rental pays and, on a condo, the dues decide most deals.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is a Myrtle Beach condo a good investment?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only if the rent still covers the dues. Of 1,785 condos we tested, 214 pass the 1 percent rule on price, and 31 to 46 once the dues are counted.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax rate on a rental in Horry County?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A rental is taxed on 6 percent of its value and pays the school operating tax. For 2026 that is 201.0 mills outside city limits, about $1,206 a year for each $100,000 of value, and 254.6 mills in the City of Myrtle Beach.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you run numbers on a property listed with another brokerage?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. Any home on the Grand Strand, listed with any brokerage. We use the listing, the county record, nearby rentals and the association's papers.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is running the numbers free?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. There is no fee and no obligation. You can send one address or several.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HUD Fair Market Rents</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County 2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c043.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-43</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t12c037.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 12-37</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/tax-payer-services/real-property-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County real property tax</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer/24" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County parcels</a>, <a href="https://www.irs.gov/publications/p527" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IRS Publication 527</a>, <a href="https://www.iii.org/article/coverage-for-renting-out-your-home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Insurance Information Institute</a>. Homes for sale: asking prices, counted in aggregate from the Coastal Carolinas Association of REALTORS® MLS (CCMLS). Resales: county deeds and parcel values, read by Chapter3. Estimates for a buying decision, not an appraisal or a loan quote.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Houses in Carolina Forest from above. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut a 1600 x 1200 px view from one NOAA map tile, raised the contrast and color slightly, and resized it.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/invest-run-the-numbers/carolina-forest-houses-from-above-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/invest-run-the-numbers/carolina-forest-houses-from-above-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"Streets of houses in The Parks of Carolina Forest, the area of the example sheet, from above","caption":"Streets of houses in The Parks of Carolina Forest, the area of the example sheet, from above.","description":"Rows of similar houses with gray roofs, short driveways and small fenced back yards along curving streets in Carolina Forest, seen from above","creator":{"@type":"Organization","name":"NOAA National Geodetic Survey"},"creditText":"NOAA National Geodetic Survey, public domain","copyrightNotice":"Public domain (NOAA National Geodetic Survey)","license":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm","acquireLicensePage":"https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/","isBasedOn":"https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/","contentLocation":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Parks of Carolina Forest, Carolina Forest, Myrtle Beach, South Carolina"},"representativeOfPage":true}]}</script></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Send one address.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">We send back the sheet for that home the same day: the rent, the tax at the rate you will pay, the dues, an insurance quote, and what is left.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="#run-form">Send the address</a></div></section></main>
